Sample size of one is pretty irrelevant, a lot of people can get to
75-80% success rate with the racket and it wouldn't be too surprising
to see you succeed with 4-5 in a row.

The thing is that without it you can be much more successful; the key
to high percentage play in Nethack is getting rid of sheer random
chances for death and keeping you in the position where you have a
chance to think about every threat and deal with it.

Even without the racket, my last (only?) death in rkrobin (where I was
doing all of the early game for a good while) was because of an early
attack wand that a gnome zapped me with before I had a chance to get
enough HP to turn such random occurances into something I can deal
with.

The traditional protection racket doesn't allow that, it keeps random
wands, rolling boulders, etc as kill possibilities instead of making
them something the player can deal with.

Eliminate instadeaths ruthlessly.  In the early game, every /fire,
/lightning, rolling boulder, etc is a potential instadeath.



